# Pressure methods · numerical-coarse · C53 CUDA

Retrospective source review · fit-29706aa9da6fd913

Authored interpretation of captured source and receipts. No new training, benchmark, lineage or scientific promotion is implied.

**Method.** A hybrid pressure request: an F64 Galerkin solve on at most 4 aggregate centres per axis precedes each learned fine correction. Clamped trilinear interpolation defines P; transpose restriction and the fixed-gauge Cholesky solve use P-transpose L P. The fine CNN retains 370,016 learned coefficients. Restriction, numerical solve, prolongation, residual assembly and neural correction all belong to the configured pressure call. F64 physical residual scaling q=(rho/h)r, gauging and pressure accumulation surround the F32 learned stages. The result is pressure only; two internal corrections do not produce two physical simulation states.

**Purpose.** Test a 4-node-per-axis numerical coarse stage during both fitting and deployment, with the retained C53 fine CNN.

**Experiment.** 1,600 CUDA Adam updates, batch one, initial fine rate 1e-05, schedule [{'update': 1201, 'learning_rate': 1e-06}, {'update': 1501, 'learning_rate': 1e-07}], model seed 2026101803, index seed 2026101804. 20 physical training trajectories/40 requests; grid-density counts {'8.0': 10, '16.0': 10}. Actual tier exposure {'32': 534, '64': 533, '16': 533} and sampled voxel count 157,852,608; 3,200 fine-network root forwards. Executed added coarse/head learning-rate multiplier 1. All inherited manufactured/direction/current-policy banks are disabled; C53 fine initialization and fixed scales are retained. Physical dt remains 1/60 s and fluid density 1000 kg/m3.

**Observed outcome.** Retained final fitting loss 12.555362285390332. Common 128 consumed requests: worst mean-free pressure relative L2 0.0044392805138834214, equation relative L2 0.0008588754937347028, median case-median complete GPU pressure call 6.5043760000000006 ms. The captured default call includes its declared numerical/learned stages, CPU input/output, transfers and synchronization. Cached geometry is warmed; setup/first calls/scoring are separate. These are pressure-request observations, not full-step latency, independent holdout evidence or own-history drift. No new model execution is added.

**Lesson.** A parameter count describes only the learned part of this hybrid. Numerical work and geometry preparation require separate accounting. C94/C95 isolate four/six-node stages under matched retained exposure; comparisons to earlier C83 also change data and training budget.

**Reproduction.** Retain the exact typed evidence recipe, witnessed model/preprocessing/coarse sources, method specifications, optimizer group policy, runtime, physical views, fixed scales and transformed C53 initialization. Reproduce the exact private tier/replay stream, including preserved small draws and all large-grid voxel work. Numerical stages require their interpolation, gauge and cached-geometry policy; learned stages require gains, gating and any shape-head initialization. Historical publication/restore has CPU neural calls: qualify GPU-only equivalents before rerunning. Clean fitting, new-Rheon generation and long own-history drift remain unqualified; preserve original receipts and historical ancestry.

